.Dd February 1, 2026
.Dt KPRINT 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm kprint
.Nd print string to kernel console
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/console.h
.Ft void
.Fn kprint "const char *str"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn kprint
function writes the null-terminated string
.Fa str
to the kernel console/log.
It is a low-level printing routine, often used by
.Xr printf 9
and for early boot debugging.
.Pp
It is safe to call from most contexts, including interrupt handlers (depending on the console driver implementation).
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr printf 9 ,
.Xr panic 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn kprint
function first appeared in Substrate.
